  "premise_review": [
    "BSDContract supplies Curve : Type, four Nat annotations and two actual Nat equalities. Preserve the entire record and both genuine exact projection proofs; none computes curve ranks or a Sha order.",
    "HasseWeilContract, ShafarevichTateContract and ModularityContract choose independent named Prop fields and supplied proofs. They define no Euler product, continuation, functional equation, Finite instance or association relation. All four genuine proof projections remain archived.",
    "BSDDataSource has actual CurveId/TwistParam types and a twist function, an actual TwistParam-indexed certification predicate, but an independent infiniteFamily Prop. AllTwistsCertified really is a universal predicate. CertifiedBSDDataSource supplies both the chosen infiniteFamily proof and the full universal certification proof. Preserve all these complete schemas and definitions without narrowing or inferring infinitude/strong BSD.",
    "bsd_data_source_certifies is the exact genuine identity proof h under its complete universal hypothesis. The two certified-source proofs are genuine projections. They remain with their mixed same-file providers; no missing legacy self-import is added.",
    "ArithmeticMonodromyParameterSource retains K/[Field K]/E plus source/relationName and bare usableForMonodromy Prop; no actual monodromy parameterization or relation is defined.",
    "Captured arithmetic dependency bodies have root-file path hints rather than the exact Arithmetic import path; no historical binding is reconstructed or claimed."
  ],
